{% doc %}
  Loads at once the images that the first screen shows.

  Each section decides in Liquid how its images load: eager when it opens the
  page (section.index 1), lazy lower down. Liquid cannot see the sections
  above, though: below a short text section, a featured blog or a multicolumn
  can stand in the first screen and hold its largest image while it still
  waits as lazy (measured 29/10/2026: the featured blog's first image, LCP of
  the page at 412, 1350 and 1920 px). Here, once the page is parsed, every
  lazy image shown inside the first screen switches to eager; an image kept
  out of sight (a card's hover view, a slide waiting its turn) stays lazy. The
  priority hints the sections set are left as they are.

  Without JavaScript, each image keeps the loading its section gave it.

  @example
  {% render 'first-screen-images' %}
{% enddoc %}
<script>
  (function () {
    'use strict';
    var fold = window.innerHeight || document.documentElement.clientHeight;
    var edge = window.innerWidth || document.documentElement.clientWidth;
    var images = document.querySelectorAll('[id^="shopify-section"] img[loading="lazy"]');
    for (var i = 0; i < images.length; i++) {
      var img = images[i];
      var box = img.getBoundingClientRect();
      if (!box.width || !box.height || box.top >= fold || box.bottom <= 0 || box.left >= edge || box.right <= 0) continue;
      // A picture waiting for its turn (a card's hover view, a slide behind
      // the current one) is not on screen yet.
      var style = getComputedStyle(img);
      if (style.opacity === '0' || style.visibility === 'hidden') continue;
      img.loading = 'eager';
    }
  })();
</script>
